## Grok-cli quirks worth knowing

- TUI renders to stderr (not stdout) — if you spawn grok in a tmux pane, do NOT redirect stderr to a file or the TUI will be invisible.
- Boots to a modal session menu (New worktree / Resume session / Quit) — your bootstrap script needs to send `Ctrl-S` to reach the chat REPL.
- Submit key in input-ready mode is plain Enter, NOT Kitty CSI-u Enter (that toggles modes).
- Daemon's full-body injection mode is required (fleet-notify v1.0.1+) because grok-cli doesn't honor `additionalContext` from prompt hooks the way Claude Code does.
